1
00:00:00,968 --> 00:00:05,497
<i>- Previously on</i> Gotham...
- Gotham falls, we rise.

2
00:00:09,643 --> 00:00:10,883
GORDON: <i>After the bridges blew,</i>

3
00:00:11,078 --> 00:00:12,546
<i>the city was up for grabs.</i>

4
00:00:14,047 --> 00:00:16,175
<i>Gangs are carving up territory.</i>

5
00:00:17,017 --> 00:00:18,747
(screams)

6
00:00:19,086 --> 00:00:20,247
We are running out of food.

7
00:00:21,054 --> 00:00:22,078
(shouting)

8
00:00:22,389 --> 00:00:23,389
<i>Ammunition.</i>

9
00:00:23,690 --> 00:00:25,682
We are surrounded
by hostile forces.

10
00:00:30,397 --> 00:00:32,593
Say hello to Butch.

11
00:00:36,537 --> 00:00:38,665
(screams)

12
00:00:39,473 --> 00:00:40,338
Put out the word.

13
00:00:40,474 --> 00:00:42,272
100,000 rounds of ammunition

14
00:00:42,409 --> 00:00:44,435
to whoever kills Jim Gordon.

15
00:00:47,180 --> 00:00:48,239
(siren wails)

16
00:00:48,615 --> 00:00:49,735
NURSE: <i>You want to cure her?</i>

17
00:00:50,017 --> 00:00:51,294
(whispering): You
have to go to the witch.

18
00:00:51,318 --> 00:00:53,253
And where do I find this witch?

19
00:00:54,421 --> 00:00:55,616
You have to help us.

20
00:00:56,189 --> 00:00:57,782
My brothers and sisters,

21
00:00:58,325 --> 00:00:59,325
they're killing us.

22
00:01:03,297 --> 00:01:04,788
GORDON: <i>His name is Will Thomas.</i>

23
00:01:05,132 --> 00:01:06,464
Parents died in a home invasion

24
00:01:06,567 --> 00:01:08,433
a few weeks after the
bridges came down.

25
00:01:09,169 --> 00:01:09,795
Guys that broke in

26
00:01:10,137 --> 00:01:11,628
took him to some sort of factory

27
00:01:11,772 --> 00:01:14,640
where he was held alongside
dozens of other stolen kids,

28
00:01:15,242 --> 00:01:16,403
all chained together.

29
00:01:16,710 --> 00:01:17,710
BULLOCK: God.

30
00:01:18,145 --> 00:01:19,340
Who are these guys?

31
00:01:20,047 --> 00:01:21,743
Call themselves The Soothsayers.

32
00:01:22,282 --> 00:01:24,183
- You ever heard of them?
- No.

33
00:01:24,451 --> 00:01:25,817
But who can keep
track these days?

34
00:01:26,153 --> 00:01:28,247
- Which district?
- Granton. Near the water,

35
00:01:28,355 --> 00:01:30,790
he said. Had them
digging some sort of tunnel.

36
00:01:31,224 --> 00:01:33,193
Will broke free from
his restraints last night

37
00:01:33,327 --> 00:01:36,195
and walked nine miles
through the Dark Zone to find us.

38
00:01:36,330 --> 00:01:37,662
What kind of tunnel?

39
00:01:38,065 --> 00:01:39,260
Unclear.

40
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:43,798
There's an abandoned waterworks
by the old dock in Granton.

41
00:01:44,671 --> 00:01:45,798
Detective Gordon?

42
00:01:48,742 --> 00:01:50,233
My friends.

43
00:01:50,510 --> 00:01:52,536
You'll save them, won't you?

44
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:55,248
I'll look into it.

45
00:01:56,083 --> 00:01:58,314
The Soothsayers won't
be happy I escaped.

46
00:01:59,186 --> 00:02:00,620
They'll punish
the others for it.

47
00:02:02,255 --> 00:02:03,416
Please, Mr. Gordon.

48
00:02:03,557 --> 00:02:05,321
I promised them I'd bring help.

49
00:02:08,428 --> 00:02:10,795
I know it's a sad story
and emotions are high,

50
00:02:11,131 --> 00:02:13,209
but need I remind you that
every two-bit criminal out there

51
00:02:13,233 --> 00:02:14,744
is looking to kill you to
claim Penguin's bounty?

52
00:02:14,768 --> 00:02:16,008
So you're saying we do nothing?

53
00:02:16,203 --> 00:02:18,081
No, I'm saying the second
you step outside that door,

54
00:02:18,105 --> 00:02:19,282
someone's gonna
take a shot at you,

55
00:02:19,306 --> 00:02:20,583
and if it's not you
that's getting hit,

56
00:02:20,607 --> 00:02:22,251
it's gonna be the schmo
standing next to you,

57
00:02:22,275 --> 00:02:23,675
which is most
likely gonna be me.

58
00:02:24,177 --> 00:02:25,177
Captain.

59
00:02:25,646 --> 00:02:27,114
There's a call
from the mainland.

60
00:02:29,616 --> 00:02:30,693
MAN: <i>All of us here believe</i>

61
00:02:30,717 --> 00:02:33,118
<i>that if peace is to be
sustained on the island,</i>

62
00:02:33,253 --> 00:02:34,778
<i>confrontations must be avoided.</i>

63
00:02:35,222 --> 00:02:37,282
We have kids in
danger out there.

64
00:02:37,691 --> 00:02:39,387
We're their only
hope for rescue.

65
00:02:39,726 --> 00:02:41,838
MAN: <i>Your dedication to
your job is admirable, Captain,</i>

66
00:02:41,862 --> 00:02:43,455
<i>but you lack perspective.</i>

67
00:02:43,597 --> 00:02:45,677
<i>Travel into harm's way,
and you may save a few lives,</i>

68
00:02:45,799 --> 00:02:47,267
<i>but you'd also be jeopardizing</i>

69
00:02:47,401 --> 00:02:49,870
<i>thousands of others
should you be killed.</i>

70
00:02:50,203 --> 00:02:52,468
<i>The collective opinion over
here is that you stand down</i>

71
00:02:52,606 --> 00:02:54,666
<i>and keep those within
your Green Zone safe.</i>

72
00:02:54,875 --> 00:02:56,639
I don't need opinions,
I need supplies.

73
00:02:56,777 --> 00:02:58,245
When can I expect them?

74
00:02:58,478 --> 00:03:00,879
MAN: <i>Until Gotham airspace
can be declared safe again,</i>

75
00:03:01,214 --> 00:03:03,308
<i>we cannot sacrifice
any more pilots,</i>

76
00:03:03,450 --> 00:03:05,578
<i>whether they're ours
or Wayne Enterprises'.</i>

77
00:03:06,420 --> 00:03:08,580
So you can save a few lives
for thousands, but I can't?

78
00:03:08,655 --> 00:03:09,918
MAN: <i>Mr. Gordon...</i>

79
00:03:17,164 --> 00:03:18,164
BULLOCK: Jim.

80
00:03:19,866 --> 00:03:22,529
I need five men and
transport for 20 kids or more.

81
00:03:22,936 --> 00:03:24,268
We only have a few squad cars

82
00:03:24,404 --> 00:03:26,604
- and that rust bucket
transporter.
- That'll have to do.

83
00:03:26,707 --> 00:03:27,572
How are we on ammo?

84
00:03:27,708 --> 00:03:29,152
Well, we got what
we got from Penguin,

85
00:03:29,176 --> 00:03:30,667
and we got a box
of shotgun shells

86
00:03:30,811 --> 00:03:31,811
and a box of nine mils.

87
00:03:31,912 --> 00:03:33,676
What did the bureaucrats
on the mainland say?

88
00:03:33,814 --> 00:03:35,282
Do nothing, protect
the Green Zone.

89
00:03:35,716 --> 00:03:36,716
Four shells each.

90
00:03:36,783 --> 00:03:37,910
Half a mag each.

91
00:03:38,685 --> 00:03:40,313
Boy said The
Soothsayers are here.

92
00:03:40,454 --> 00:03:42,494
That means we have to
pass through Sirens territory,

93
00:03:42,589 --> 00:03:44,429
but it's only three or
four miles from then on.

94
00:03:44,458 --> 00:03:46,256
Three or four miles
into the Dark Zone?

95
00:03:46,593 --> 00:03:47,891
God only knows what's out there.

96
00:03:48,562 --> 00:03:49,922
Barbara's been
stockpiling vehicles

97
00:03:50,230 --> 00:03:52,150
and everything else as
payment to enter her club.

98
00:03:52,199 --> 00:03:53,743
- It's worth a shot.
- She's gonna be thrilled

99
00:03:53,767 --> 00:03:55,929
to see you after what
happened with Tabitha.

100
00:03:56,737 --> 00:03:58,781
We're gonna need housing
for those kids when we get back.

101
00:03:58,805 --> 00:04:00,501
- Yep.
<i>- If</i> we get back.

102
00:04:05,812 --> 00:04:07,781
(dog barking in distance)

103
00:04:18,391 --> 00:04:20,553
(gate creaks)

104
00:04:29,569 --> 00:04:31,504
(insects trilling)

105
00:04:45,285 --> 00:04:46,981
♪♪

106
00:04:56,329 --> 00:04:58,264
(water dripping)

107
00:05:17,050 --> 00:05:18,951
♪♪

108
00:05:43,910 --> 00:05:45,572
(footsteps approaching)

109
00:05:46,980 --> 00:05:48,471
(panting)

110
00:05:48,615 --> 00:05:50,015
MAN: Let him go.

111
00:05:56,890 --> 00:05:59,018
- Are you with her?
- Who?

112
00:06:00,327 --> 00:06:01,488
The witch.

113
00:06:03,797 --> 00:06:05,459
I'm not with the witch.

114
00:06:05,599 --> 00:06:06,828
I just came here for her help.

115
00:06:06,967 --> 00:06:08,629
Come for her magic, have you?

116
00:06:09,369 --> 00:06:10,769
So did others from our district.

117
00:06:11,004 --> 00:06:12,404
And look at them now.

118
00:06:12,739 --> 00:06:13,866
They came for help, too,

119
00:06:14,007 --> 00:06:15,407
and she took their souls.

120
00:06:16,543 --> 00:06:17,909
But she'll never kill again.

121
00:06:18,445 --> 00:06:19,674
We have her this time.

122
00:06:20,046 --> 00:06:21,046
You captured her?

123
00:06:21,081 --> 00:06:22,681
She's locked in the
storeroom back there.

124
00:06:22,949 --> 00:06:25,509
We stripped it clean
before we locked her in.

125
00:06:26,653 --> 00:06:28,645
The plants, you see.

126
00:06:30,023 --> 00:06:31,355
She talks to them.

127
00:06:32,425 --> 00:06:33,723
Makes them do things.

128
00:06:35,695 --> 00:06:38,756
So we took her light,
water; put salt on the floor.

129
00:06:39,599 --> 00:06:40,897
She's helpless now.

130
00:06:41,434 --> 00:06:42,434
I need to talk to her.

131
00:06:42,469 --> 00:06:44,495
No. We sent

132
00:06:44,638 --> 00:06:45,765
for more of us.

133
00:06:46,106 --> 00:06:48,940
When they come, we burn her.

134
00:06:52,946 --> 00:06:53,970
Listen.

135
00:06:54,714 --> 00:06:56,012
My brother is missing.

136
00:06:56,149 --> 00:06:57,913
I know this witch took him.

137
00:06:58,485 --> 00:07:00,420
I need to find out
what she did with him.

138
00:07:01,087 --> 00:07:03,420
Please, let me talk to her.
Five minutes is all I need,

139
00:07:03,556 --> 00:07:05,036
and then you can do
whatever you want.

140
00:07:05,625 --> 00:07:07,025
Your brother's dead.

141
00:07:07,794 --> 00:07:09,456
She'll kill you, too.

142
00:07:10,497 --> 00:07:11,760
Five minutes.

143
00:07:16,536 --> 00:07:17,536
In there.

144
00:07:33,853 --> 00:07:35,617
Hello, Ivy.

145
00:07:37,490 --> 00:07:39,186
♪♪

146
00:07:43,763 --> 00:07:47,461
♪ Love is a burning thing ♪

147
00:07:48,168 --> 00:07:50,137
♪ And it makes ♪

148
00:07:50,503 --> 00:07:52,972
♪ A fiery ring ♪

149
00:07:54,174 --> 00:07:58,043
♪ Bound by wild desire ♪

150
00:07:59,713 --> 00:08:03,206
♪ I fell into a ring of fire ♪

151
00:08:04,918 --> 00:08:06,910
♪ I fell into... ♪

152
00:08:07,087 --> 00:08:08,180
Barbara.

153
00:08:08,888 --> 00:08:11,187
This place is busy,
despite things.

154
00:08:12,592 --> 00:08:13,592
What's that?

155
00:08:13,626 --> 00:08:14,826
♪ And the flames went higher ♪

156
00:08:14,928 --> 00:08:18,456
It's a big fat prize, Jim,
begging to be taken.

157
00:08:19,666 --> 00:08:21,897
So, what brings you crawling
out into the open tonight?

158
00:08:22,202 --> 00:08:23,202
Come to join the party?

159
00:08:23,236 --> 00:08:25,603
One last hoorah before
someone wastes you?

160
00:08:25,872 --> 00:08:26,872
I'm here to ask a favor.

161
00:08:26,973 --> 00:08:27,973
(laughs)

162
00:08:29,175 --> 00:08:31,701
A favor, right. Is this after

163
00:08:31,845 --> 00:08:33,711
you stood by and did nothing

164
00:08:34,147 --> 00:08:35,775
while my best
friend on this Earth

165
00:08:35,915 --> 00:08:37,115
was stabbed through the heart?

166
00:08:37,183 --> 00:08:39,243
- I put him down.
- You restored his limp.

167
00:08:39,586 --> 00:08:41,020
- He should be dead!
- Barbara.

168
00:08:41,154 --> 00:08:42,782
Everybody out!

169
00:08:42,922 --> 00:08:45,118
- Now!
- (music stops)

170
00:08:45,792 --> 00:08:47,590
I said move!

171
00:08:50,697 --> 00:08:51,995
Planning revenge?

172
00:08:52,932 --> 00:08:56,061
Well, someone has to do
something about that freak.

173
00:08:57,137 --> 00:08:59,629
He has an army.
It would be suicide.

174
00:09:01,007 --> 00:09:02,007
Look around, Jim.

175
00:09:04,244 --> 00:09:06,076
We're all slowly dying.

176
00:09:07,147 --> 00:09:09,548
Just some of us
get to choose how.

177
00:09:10,717 --> 00:09:13,243
I'm sorry about what
happened to Tabitha.

178
00:09:13,987 --> 00:09:15,512
Things got out of control.

179
00:09:15,655 --> 00:09:18,181
I'm just trying to keep
this city from falling apart.

180
00:09:26,566 --> 00:09:27,566
You're too late.

181
00:09:33,106 --> 00:09:34,199
So, this favor?

182
00:09:36,609 --> 00:09:37,907
I need transportation.

183
00:09:38,578 --> 00:09:40,809
- Trucks, maybe.
- Where are you going?

184
00:09:40,947 --> 00:09:42,813
- It's a police matter.
- (laughs softly)

185
00:09:45,085 --> 00:09:47,987
You know, they should really
write that on your tombstone.

186
00:09:49,556 --> 00:09:50,556
(chuckles)

187
00:09:50,657 --> 00:09:52,101
They're downstairs
in the basement lot.

188
00:09:52,125 --> 00:09:53,252
Knock yourself out.

189
00:09:53,893 --> 00:09:56,761
Drive right into this
nightmare you created.

190
00:09:57,764 --> 00:09:58,959
You won't last the night.

191
00:10:01,668 --> 00:10:02,931
Here he comes, Gotham.

192
00:10:03,636 --> 00:10:07,664
Your judge, your jailer,
your most hated son!

193
00:10:07,874 --> 00:10:08,874
Have at him!

194
00:10:09,175 --> 00:10:11,076
Rip him to shreds!

195
00:10:14,147 --> 00:10:15,274
(door closes)

196
00:10:15,882 --> 00:10:18,317
No one deserves
to die more than he.

197
00:10:33,333 --> 00:10:35,244
BULLOCK: <i>All right, we're
entering the Dark Zone.</i>

198
00:10:35,268 --> 00:10:36,998
<i>Everybody, stay sharp.</i>

199
00:10:49,382 --> 00:10:50,748
<i>This place was a cesspit</i>

200
00:10:50,884 --> 00:10:53,183
before the rest of the
world turned its back on us.

201
00:10:53,319 --> 00:10:54,810
I wonder what's left here now.

202
00:10:54,954 --> 00:10:56,616
I doubt many stayed up here.

203
00:10:57,323 --> 00:10:59,724
This whole grid
never regained power.

204
00:11:04,264 --> 00:11:05,391
(glass breaking)

205
00:11:07,233 --> 00:11:10,226
(shouting)

206
00:11:10,670 --> 00:11:12,832
Damn it! You were saying, Jim?

207
00:11:15,074 --> 00:11:16,133
(shouts)

208
00:11:16,843 --> 00:11:18,209
It's a freaking arrow, Jim.

209
00:11:18,845 --> 00:11:20,643
It's a freaking arrow!

210
00:11:22,015 --> 00:11:23,677
Welcome to the badlands.

211
00:11:47,040 --> 00:11:48,269
(grunts) Come on.

212
00:11:48,675 --> 00:11:50,268
- Come on, come on.
- (groans softly)

213
00:11:50,410 --> 00:11:51,935
- Get up!
- Aah!

214
00:11:52,078 --> 00:11:53,239
Come on!

215
00:11:53,746 --> 00:11:54,746
Hey! Hey, hey, hey.

216
00:11:54,847 --> 00:11:56,076
Leave him alone.

217
00:11:58,184 --> 00:12:00,016
Causing trouble again, Gabriel?

218
00:12:00,220 --> 00:12:02,951
We need water and food.
Some of us haven't slept

219
00:12:03,089 --> 00:12:04,717
in two days.

220
00:12:05,992 --> 00:12:07,232
You know, you could've woken me

221
00:12:07,260 --> 00:12:09,729
when that sneaky
rat left in the night.

222
00:12:11,397 --> 00:12:14,196
But you didn't, and
now, he's out there,

223
00:12:14,334 --> 00:12:16,462
and he's causing all
kinds of problems for us.

224
00:12:23,076 --> 00:12:25,978
(exhales) The smoke.

225
00:12:26,112 --> 00:12:27,705
You should take it.

226
00:12:28,414 --> 00:12:29,882
It'll give you energy.

227
00:12:30,950 --> 00:12:32,145
Inhale enough...

228
00:12:33,853 --> 00:12:35,719
and it'll let you
see the future.

229
00:12:41,261 --> 00:12:44,356
You fail to see the importance
of our work here, Gabriel.

230
00:12:44,764 --> 00:12:47,290
But you see, once
this tunnel is complete,

231
00:12:47,467 --> 00:12:50,437
we will have exclusive
access to the mainland.

232
00:12:51,204 --> 00:12:54,038
People will be forced
to do business with us.

233
00:12:54,173 --> 00:12:56,733
Food, booze, guns,

234
00:12:57,243 --> 00:12:58,370
smoke.

235
00:12:59,345 --> 00:13:02,907
All will come from the tunnel.

236
00:13:03,383 --> 00:13:05,147
We've been digging
for over a month.

237
00:13:05,285 --> 00:13:06,810
We've only gotten
a hundred feet.

238
00:13:07,453 --> 00:13:08,453
It's too narrow.

239
00:13:08,788 --> 00:13:10,950
The roof is leaking. Once
we hit the river, it'll flood

240
00:13:11,090 --> 00:13:13,116
- and kill anyone inside.
- So negative!

241
00:13:13,293 --> 00:13:14,386
Gabriel.

242
00:13:15,028 --> 00:13:16,028
Shame.

243
00:13:17,063 --> 00:13:19,225
I had such high hopes for you.

244
00:13:20,166 --> 00:13:24,126
That one day you would
wear the mask and share

245
00:13:24,270 --> 00:13:26,136
in our good fortune.

246
00:13:26,806 --> 00:13:28,069
Never mind.

247
00:13:29,108 --> 00:13:29,837
MAN: Sykes.

248
00:13:29,976 --> 00:13:31,342
Man, you got to come out front.

249
00:13:44,891 --> 00:13:46,086
Who was on watch?!

250
00:13:46,893 --> 00:13:48,225
GORDON: Put your weapons down.

251
00:13:52,031 --> 00:13:53,932
Is that James Gordon?

252
00:13:56,102 --> 00:13:58,094
<i>The</i> James Gordon?

253
00:14:01,107 --> 00:14:02,837
It's our lucky day, fellas.

254
00:14:03,176 --> 00:14:05,145
Kill this one, and
we're bullet rich!

255
00:14:06,479 --> 00:14:08,311
In Penguin's graces we will be.

256
00:14:08,448 --> 00:14:10,417
(guns clicking)

257
00:14:15,822 --> 00:14:16,949
I said put 'em down.

258
00:14:29,102 --> 00:14:30,102
Give us the kids

259
00:14:30,136 --> 00:14:31,934
you're holding
captive. We'll leave.

260
00:14:32,372 --> 00:14:33,372
Kids?

261
00:14:34,507 --> 00:14:36,027
I don't know what
you're talking about.

262
00:14:36,509 --> 00:14:38,171
What are the cattle prods for?

263
00:14:41,214 --> 00:14:42,307
Fun.

264
00:14:50,390 --> 00:14:51,390
Stay here.

265
00:14:51,591 --> 00:14:53,890
He moves, kill him.

266
00:15:04,971 --> 00:15:06,132
It's okay.

267
00:15:06,873 --> 00:15:08,307
It's all right. I'm a cop.

268
00:15:10,476 --> 00:15:11,603
Will's alive?

269
00:15:13,079 --> 00:15:14,523
He found you and sent
you to rescue us, didn't he?

270
00:15:14,547 --> 00:15:15,547
He did.

271
00:15:16,149 --> 00:15:17,344
Will made it! He's alive!

272
00:15:17,450 --> 00:15:19,942
- (cheering)
- We need the keys.

273
00:15:21,187 --> 00:15:22,883
There are trucks outside.

274
00:15:23,389 --> 00:15:25,017
We'll drive you to
the Green Zone,

275
00:15:25,525 --> 00:15:26,525
find you a new home.

276
00:15:26,592 --> 00:15:28,185
Thank you. God bless you.

277
00:15:29,495 --> 00:15:31,430
Okay, guys. We're
gonna get out of here.

278
00:15:31,564 --> 00:15:33,465
Gonna help us get
out. One at a time.

279
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:35,964
Yeah, we're gonna be okay.

280
00:15:37,103 --> 00:15:39,436
Why would anyone be
a cop in a world like this?

281
00:15:39,639 --> 00:15:42,302
Well, the Halloween shop
was all out of gas masks,

282
00:15:42,442 --> 00:15:45,970
so it was either
this or sexy nurse.

283
00:15:50,983 --> 00:15:51,983
You know what?

284
00:15:52,084 --> 00:15:55,577
My guess is these cops ain't
got enough ammo to shoot a duck.

285
00:15:55,922 --> 00:15:58,585
Wrong. Penguin
gave us a boatload.

286
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:01,223
Penguin wants your boss skinned.

287
00:16:01,494 --> 00:16:02,689
Let's take 'em, boys.

288
00:16:05,364 --> 00:16:06,593
Come on! Go! Go!

289
00:16:06,933 --> 00:16:08,401
(gunfire)

290
00:16:08,534 --> 00:16:09,558
(Bullock yells)

291
00:16:14,674 --> 00:16:17,007
(gunfire continues)

292
00:16:20,580 --> 00:16:21,580
Hey!

293
00:16:23,082 --> 00:16:23,708
Go!

294
00:16:24,050 --> 00:16:25,211
(child screams)

295
00:16:25,284 --> 00:16:26,946
Gabriel!

296
00:16:30,189 --> 00:16:31,953
You okay? Come on.

297
00:16:38,598 --> 00:16:41,625
- Take cover! Go! Go!
- (whimpers)

298
00:16:45,271 --> 00:16:47,740
- The alley! Go! Go!
- Come on!

299
00:16:58,584 --> 00:17:00,246
(yelling)

300
00:17:15,234 --> 00:17:16,566
(gasps softly)

301
00:17:19,539 --> 00:17:20,539
Bruce?

302
00:17:21,007 --> 00:17:22,134
(sighs)

303
00:17:22,375 --> 00:17:23,673
Thank God.

304
00:17:25,478 --> 00:17:27,106
You have to help me.

305
00:17:29,549 --> 00:17:32,280
I didn't kill those men
out there in the vines,

306
00:17:32,418 --> 00:17:34,182
- you have to believe me.
- You'll forgive me

307
00:17:34,353 --> 00:17:36,117
if I find it hard to do so.

308
00:17:38,491 --> 00:17:40,050
It wasn't me.

309
00:17:42,461 --> 00:17:43,461
It was the park.

310
00:17:43,763 --> 00:17:44,763
The park?

311
00:17:45,097 --> 00:17:49,034
The trees, the plants, the roots

312
00:17:49,168 --> 00:17:50,261
underground...

313
00:17:51,237 --> 00:17:53,138
They're speaking to one another.

314
00:17:54,607 --> 00:17:56,235
When those men
came to kill me...

315
00:17:56,375 --> 00:17:57,775
(panting)

316
00:17:58,110 --> 00:18:00,238
the plants came
to my protection.

317
00:18:05,117 --> 00:18:06,517
Then maybe we
can help each other.

318
00:18:07,420 --> 00:18:08,615
I have...

319
00:18:09,789 --> 00:18:12,418
a friend... who was shot.

320
00:18:12,692 --> 00:18:14,217
The bullet severed
her spinal cord.

321
00:18:14,327 --> 00:18:16,091
The doctors can't
seem to help her.

322
00:18:16,729 --> 00:18:19,062
But a woman at the hospital
said that you might be able to.

323
00:18:20,366 --> 00:18:22,335
Normally, I would say no.

324
00:18:24,737 --> 00:18:27,172
But this park... ever
since we were cut off

325
00:18:27,306 --> 00:18:29,707
from the rest of the world,
it's been behaving differently.

326
00:18:31,611 --> 00:18:33,136
There are things growing here

327
00:18:33,279 --> 00:18:34,611
I have never seen before.

328
00:18:34,747 --> 00:18:36,579
- (knocking)
- MAN:
You okay in there?

329
00:18:37,283 --> 00:18:38,581
Our friends are on their way.

330
00:18:39,218 --> 00:18:40,777
Time's running
out for you, witch!

331
00:18:44,223 --> 00:18:45,282
There's a seed.

332
00:18:48,094 --> 00:18:49,653
It's growing under the oaks.

333
00:18:51,230 --> 00:18:53,256
It's said to have
magical qualities.

334
00:18:53,866 --> 00:18:55,095
When digested, it heads

335
00:18:55,234 --> 00:18:57,169
for damaged tissue
and bone, healing them.

336
00:18:58,871 --> 00:19:00,533
If I help you find it...

337
00:19:02,708 --> 00:19:05,177
will you protect me from
those men out there?

338
00:19:21,560 --> 00:19:22,560
(gasps)

339
00:19:27,433 --> 00:19:29,163
(chains rattle)

340
00:19:31,570 --> 00:19:34,369
Yes! Yes!

341
00:19:34,573 --> 00:19:35,836
Yes, it worked!

342
00:19:36,509 --> 00:19:39,172
No... more...

343
00:19:39,311 --> 00:19:41,280
sleepwalking for me.

344
00:19:42,348 --> 00:19:43,372
(sighs)

345
00:19:44,216 --> 00:19:45,445
Good morning.

346
00:19:49,488 --> 00:19:50,217
(zipper opens)

347
00:19:50,356 --> 00:19:51,380
(sighs)

348
00:19:51,791 --> 00:19:54,158
See, it was just some...

349
00:19:55,261 --> 00:19:57,162
random stupid thing
brought on by stress.

350
00:19:57,296 --> 00:19:58,924
(urinating)

351
00:19:59,265 --> 00:20:00,733
It's all in your head.

352
00:20:06,539 --> 00:20:09,338
(man groaning)

353
00:20:16,449 --> 00:20:17,781
There's nothing there.

354
00:20:18,684 --> 00:20:21,210
(laughs)

355
00:20:23,222 --> 00:20:25,248
(sighs)

356
00:20:25,658 --> 00:20:27,286
(man groaning)

357
00:20:31,964 --> 00:20:32,964
(zipper closes)

358
00:20:35,735 --> 00:20:37,966
- (gasps)
- Who the hell are you?

359
00:20:39,638 --> 00:20:41,800
What? Are you serious?

360
00:20:41,974 --> 00:20:42,974
Very.

361
00:20:43,442 --> 00:20:44,603
You don't remember?

362
00:20:44,810 --> 00:20:46,711
- No.
- Oh.

363
00:20:47,513 --> 00:20:48,776
Name's Tank.

364
00:20:51,217 --> 00:20:52,697
You're part of the
Street Demonz gang?

365
00:20:53,953 --> 00:20:54,784
Yeah.

366
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:55,979
You know that.

367
00:20:56,722 --> 00:20:57,849
Why should I?

368
00:20:59,592 --> 00:21:00,719
What are you doing here?

369
00:21:01,527 --> 00:21:02,927
You brought me here.

370
00:21:03,496 --> 00:21:05,488
- I brought you here?
- Last night.

371
00:21:07,566 --> 00:21:08,966
Did I, uh...

372
00:21:09,301 --> 00:21:10,929
hit you, et cetera?

373
00:21:13,639 --> 00:21:14,937
Any idea why?

374
00:21:15,708 --> 00:21:16,869
You wanted information,

375
00:21:17,476 --> 00:21:19,240
and I wouldn't give it to you.

376
00:21:21,347 --> 00:21:23,009
I'm gonna guess
you gave it to me.

377
00:21:23,716 --> 00:21:26,709
Huh. I can't remember.

378
00:21:29,288 --> 00:21:31,314
We're gonna have to do
this all again, aren't we?

379
00:21:32,424 --> 00:21:33,653
Guess so.

380
00:21:35,261 --> 00:21:36,261
Fine.

381
00:21:38,731 --> 00:21:41,462
SYKES: Gordon, where are you?

382
00:21:41,934 --> 00:21:43,300
We need to hide.

383
00:21:45,838 --> 00:21:46,931
Follow me.

384
00:21:52,011 --> 00:21:53,946
(door creaks closed)

385
00:21:58,984 --> 00:22:00,350
It's not safe out there.

386
00:22:02,922 --> 00:22:03,999
We've got to get
out of the daylight.

387
00:22:04,023 --> 00:22:05,787
We're sitting ducks.
How are they holding up?

388
00:22:06,392 --> 00:22:07,392
We'll be fine.

389
00:22:07,693 --> 00:22:08,854
Jim, we're not alone.

390
00:22:09,728 --> 00:22:11,754
Someone lit that candle.

391
00:22:14,033 --> 00:22:16,525
In the old west, settlers
used to leave a candle burning

392
00:22:16,669 --> 00:22:18,501
to lead others to safety.

393
00:22:18,804 --> 00:22:20,705
Maybe there's still good
people left in Gotham.

394
00:22:22,474 --> 00:22:23,066
All right, fine.

395
00:22:23,409 --> 00:22:24,638
We'll take a look around.

396
00:22:26,312 --> 00:22:27,312
Stay here.

397
00:22:28,013 --> 00:22:29,845
If you see something, shout.

398
00:22:32,718 --> 00:22:33,718
Radio check.

399
00:22:34,053 --> 00:22:35,487
Ah, forget it.

400
00:22:35,788 --> 00:22:37,689
We're out of range of
the precinct's antenna.

401
00:22:37,890 --> 00:22:40,052
Look, if those other trucks
made it back to safety,

402
00:22:40,492 --> 00:22:42,504
maybe they'll send someone
back here to get us, huh?

403
00:22:42,528 --> 00:22:45,088
Maybe. Until then, I'll take the
next floor, you do the basement.

404
00:22:45,431 --> 00:22:48,595
Oh. Check out the basement
in a creepy hotel by myself?

405
00:22:48,734 --> 00:22:49,565
Sure.

406
00:22:49,702 --> 00:22:51,068
What could go wrong, right?

407
00:22:53,772 --> 00:22:55,035
(sighs)

408
00:23:01,046 --> 00:23:02,105
Let's get settled.

409
00:23:13,592 --> 00:23:15,493
(floorboards creaking)

410
00:23:25,804 --> 00:23:27,670
(door creaks)

411
00:23:38,150 --> 00:23:40,016
(creaking nearby)

412
00:23:42,922 --> 00:23:44,083
Hello?

413
00:23:48,994 --> 00:23:50,622
Is somebody there?

414
00:23:52,031 --> 00:23:53,090
GCPD.

415
00:23:59,638 --> 00:24:01,004
Come out, now.

416
00:24:04,576 --> 00:24:07,569
Whoa, whoa. It's
okay. It's all right.

417
00:24:11,884 --> 00:24:14,444
(fire crackling)

418
00:24:28,534 --> 00:24:30,002
♪♪

419
00:24:40,079 --> 00:24:41,479
Oh, my God.

420
00:24:41,780 --> 00:24:44,545
Oh. Not good.

421
00:24:44,683 --> 00:24:45,946
Oh, God. This...

422
00:24:46,151 --> 00:24:47,175
This is not good.

423
00:24:47,553 --> 00:24:50,887
(shouts) Jim!

424
00:24:54,460 --> 00:24:57,589
(grunts, groans)

425
00:24:58,731 --> 00:25:01,223
Fine. I'll tell you.

426
00:25:02,835 --> 00:25:05,532
You wanted to know where
the Street Demonz base was.

427
00:25:06,538 --> 00:25:07,062
That's it?

428
00:25:07,206 --> 00:25:09,675
And you wanted to be sure
the boss would be there.

429
00:25:09,808 --> 00:25:11,037
Emmanuel Vasquez?

430
00:25:11,910 --> 00:25:12,910
Yeah.

431
00:25:16,482 --> 00:25:17,482
Okay. How did I seem?

432
00:25:17,583 --> 00:25:20,781
Was I confident, flamboyant,

433
00:25:20,919 --> 00:25:21,978
charisma for days?

434
00:25:22,121 --> 00:25:23,321
Or a little more conservative,

435
00:25:23,522 --> 00:25:24,990
kind of repressed,
a little nerdy?

436
00:25:26,025 --> 00:25:28,221
You seemed stiff,
man of few words.

437
00:25:28,894 --> 00:25:30,556
In a daze, actually.

438
00:25:32,798 --> 00:25:33,925
Interesting.

439
00:25:35,167 --> 00:25:36,726
Okay, let's go.

440
00:25:37,202 --> 00:25:38,261
Where?

441
00:25:38,904 --> 00:25:40,236
To where you told me to go.

442
00:25:40,639 --> 00:25:42,107
To the Street Demonz' base.

443
00:25:42,708 --> 00:25:44,108
To Vasquez.

444
00:25:45,277 --> 00:25:47,041
I want to know why I went there.

445
00:25:58,157 --> 00:26:00,183
- Oh, no!
- Push her back inside. Lock the door.

446
00:26:00,526 --> 00:26:01,619
Stay calm.

447
00:26:02,261 --> 00:26:03,786
Okay? Her name is Ivy.

448
00:26:04,596 --> 00:26:05,596
She's a witch,

449
00:26:05,697 --> 00:26:07,063
and will burn for
what she's done.

450
00:26:07,199 --> 00:26:08,963
I take full
responsibility for her.

451
00:26:09,268 --> 00:26:10,668
If she's done what you say,

452
00:26:10,803 --> 00:26:12,203
she will pay for
her crimes, but...

453
00:26:19,111 --> 00:26:21,945
You are so utterly naive.

454
00:26:22,214 --> 00:26:23,842
You didn't have to kill them.

455
00:26:24,083 --> 00:26:25,551
I wanted to.

456
00:26:26,085 --> 00:26:27,644
Why are you here?

457
00:26:28,620 --> 00:26:29,952
I'm here for my friend.

458
00:26:30,322 --> 00:26:31,688
Our friend.

459
00:26:32,191 --> 00:26:33,191
Selina.

460
00:26:34,726 --> 00:26:36,126
Selina's the one that's hurt?

461
00:26:36,261 --> 00:26:38,787
She's paralyzed and
has lost the will to live.

462
00:26:41,900 --> 00:26:42,900
Good.

463
00:26:43,969 --> 00:26:47,167
That bitch destroyed the
last of the Lazarus Water.

464
00:26:49,174 --> 00:26:50,665
Let her suffer.

465
00:26:51,610 --> 00:26:53,101
I don't believe you mean that.

466
00:26:53,679 --> 00:26:55,090
You've known each
other for a long time.

467
00:26:55,114 --> 00:26:56,707
You grew up on
the streets together.

468
00:27:00,619 --> 00:27:04,613
You know, I wasn't lying when
I said this park is changing.

469
00:27:04,923 --> 00:27:08,758
I'm feeding the earth with
these wretched creatures.

470
00:27:09,728 --> 00:27:13,995
It consumes them,
and then it flourishes.

471
00:27:16,068 --> 00:27:18,367
I think I shall plant

472
00:27:18,704 --> 00:27:21,230
your body in the ground, Bruce.

473
00:27:23,842 --> 00:27:26,141
What will grow
from you, I wonder?

474
00:27:28,013 --> 00:27:30,175
Those men you killed were right.

475
00:27:31,717 --> 00:27:32,741
You are a witch.

476
00:27:33,252 --> 00:27:37,053
A murderous, callous witch.

477
00:27:39,158 --> 00:27:40,353
Trying to bait me, boy?

478
00:27:40,692 --> 00:27:42,217
I wouldn't waste my breath.

479
00:27:43,762 --> 00:27:45,822
I can see there's
no good left in you.

480
00:27:45,964 --> 00:27:47,899
If you were trying to
help this park flourish,

481
00:27:48,033 --> 00:27:50,195
it would be full of
beauty and color.

482
00:27:50,302 --> 00:27:52,737
Instead it smells of death.

483
00:27:54,973 --> 00:27:56,874
It's a work in progress.

484
00:27:57,376 --> 00:27:59,106
It's a nightmare.

485
00:28:01,747 --> 00:28:05,775
If I do help you,
you'll leave me alone?

486
00:28:09,721 --> 00:28:10,848
Follow me.

487
00:28:18,864 --> 00:28:19,695
It's okay.

488
00:28:19,831 --> 00:28:20,871
I'm Jim. What's your name?

489
00:28:20,966 --> 00:28:22,901
I-I can't remember.

490
00:28:23,902 --> 00:28:25,063
Where are your parents?

491
00:28:25,237 --> 00:28:26,237
Dead.

492
00:28:26,371 --> 00:28:27,839
When the lights
went out in the city,

493
00:28:28,006 --> 00:28:29,702
a gang came, they murdered them.

494
00:28:30,008 --> 00:28:31,008
I ran.

495
00:28:31,243 --> 00:28:32,336
She found me.

496
00:28:32,878 --> 00:28:33,878
Who?

497
00:28:34,146 --> 00:28:35,146
The ghost.

498
00:28:35,881 --> 00:28:37,213
She was kind at first.

499
00:28:37,783 --> 00:28:39,217
But she can be very cruel.

500
00:28:39,685 --> 00:28:40,778
BULLOCK: Jim!

501
00:28:41,153 --> 00:28:42,673
We're not alone.
There's a crazy woman.

502
00:28:42,721 --> 00:28:43,745
She's killing people.

503
00:28:43,889 --> 00:28:45,221
The ghost. We got to go.

504
00:28:45,357 --> 00:28:47,135
- She hates strangers.
- There's no such thing
as ghosts.

505
00:28:47,159 --> 00:28:48,436
We'll protect you
from whoever she is.

506
00:28:48,460 --> 00:28:49,460
You can't.

507
00:28:49,962 --> 00:28:50,986
Why? Who is she?

508
00:28:52,731 --> 00:28:54,700
She makes me call her Mother.

509
00:28:54,833 --> 00:28:55,357
We got to go.

510
00:28:55,701 --> 00:28:57,795
He's not lying! Come on, Jim.

511
00:29:04,843 --> 00:29:05,843
Hey!

512
00:29:06,378 --> 00:29:07,378
Hey!

513
00:29:07,446 --> 00:29:08,846
Come on!

514
00:29:09,081 --> 00:29:10,447
- Kid!
- (pounding on door)

515
00:29:15,821 --> 00:29:16,821
Hey, kid!

516
00:29:16,989 --> 00:29:18,252
The lights will make you dizzy.

517
00:29:18,423 --> 00:29:19,914
And then you'll fall asleep.

518
00:29:22,227 --> 00:29:23,320
You won't feel a thing.

519
00:29:24,730 --> 00:29:26,858
(groaning)

520
00:29:30,202 --> 00:29:32,137
Jim, I don't feel so good.

521
00:29:38,877 --> 00:29:40,072
(grunts)

522
00:29:42,514 --> 00:29:43,812
(door rattling)

523
00:29:46,318 --> 00:29:48,344
BOY: You can't
fight it. Give in to it.

524
00:29:53,292 --> 00:29:54,316
BULLOCK: Jim!

525
00:30:08,073 --> 00:30:09,268
(grunts)

526
00:30:10,075 --> 00:30:13,239
- Who are you?
- I'm the only mother
that boy knows.

527
00:30:13,378 --> 00:30:15,176
You're a crazy bitch
who kills people,

528
00:30:15,314 --> 00:30:17,249
takes their stuff and
burns their bodies.

529
00:30:17,382 --> 00:30:19,010
I'm protecting him.

530
00:30:19,885 --> 00:30:22,252
When I found him,
he was barely alive.

531
00:30:22,387 --> 00:30:23,514
Those animals out there,

532
00:30:23,855 --> 00:30:25,448
they would have
killed him or worse.

533
00:30:26,158 --> 00:30:28,093
I taught him how to survive.

534
00:30:28,226 --> 00:30:29,922
(both grunting)

535
00:30:35,100 --> 00:30:36,100
Hey!

536
00:30:51,016 --> 00:30:52,075
Where is everybody?

537
00:30:52,484 --> 00:30:53,281
Beats me.

538
00:30:53,418 --> 00:30:54,477
Come on.

539
00:31:02,494 --> 00:31:03,494
Oh, boy.

540
00:31:03,929 --> 00:31:05,830
TANK: Holy crap.

541
00:31:07,232 --> 00:31:08,564
That's Vasquez.

542
00:31:10,969 --> 00:31:11,993
Did you do this?

543
00:31:13,572 --> 00:31:15,302
Honestly, I don't remember.

544
00:31:16,908 --> 00:31:18,035
What about that?

545
00:31:21,613 --> 00:31:23,104
Penguin did this.

546
00:31:24,282 --> 00:31:25,580
I think not.

547
00:31:26,318 --> 00:31:30,312
Well, whoever did just
started one hell of a war.

548
00:31:47,339 --> 00:31:49,240
♪♪

549
00:32:14,399 --> 00:32:15,399
Here.

550
00:32:29,181 --> 00:32:30,376
Is that human blood?

551
00:32:30,515 --> 00:32:31,574
(laughs softly)

552
00:32:32,284 --> 00:32:34,947
If Selina ingests this, it'll
find its way to her wound.

553
00:32:35,353 --> 00:32:36,981
Its roots will wrap
around her spine,

554
00:32:37,122 --> 00:32:39,216
fusing the nerves
and cartilage together.

555
00:32:40,592 --> 00:32:41,616
It'll cure her?

556
00:32:42,561 --> 00:32:43,561
Maybe.

557
00:32:44,963 --> 00:32:45,555
Just maybe?

558
00:32:45,964 --> 00:32:47,125
Everyone's different.

559
00:32:47,265 --> 00:32:48,665
Depends on how strong she is.

560
00:32:50,602 --> 00:32:52,298
One thing is for sure though...

561
00:32:53,038 --> 00:32:54,563
The seed will alter her forever.

562
00:32:55,373 --> 00:32:57,035
- How?
- Some say

563
00:32:57,175 --> 00:33:00,304
the darker angels of our
nature are unlocked and set free.

564
00:33:05,217 --> 00:33:06,310
Can she live with that?

565
00:33:10,422 --> 00:33:11,287
Can you?

566
00:33:11,423 --> 00:33:13,221
I don't know if
there's any other way.

567
00:33:14,159 --> 00:33:15,684
Then go. Give it to her.

568
00:33:18,096 --> 00:33:19,496
What's the matter, Bruce?

569
00:33:21,032 --> 00:33:23,058
Don't know if you can trust me?

570
00:33:27,272 --> 00:33:28,706
- I don't.
- Good.

571
00:33:29,107 --> 00:33:30,632
Then you're finally
becoming a man.

572
00:33:37,482 --> 00:33:40,247
- Where will you go?
- Where I'm going
is none of your business.

573
00:33:40,752 --> 00:33:42,220
Best hurry.

574
00:33:43,421 --> 00:33:45,686
That root will die if left
out in the open for too long.

575
00:33:53,732 --> 00:33:54,732
Uh...

576
00:33:55,066 --> 00:33:57,044
Where have you guys been?
You've been gone for a while.

577
00:33:57,068 --> 00:33:58,730
Chasing ghosts.
They're like rats

578
00:33:59,070 --> 00:34:00,248
in the walls. This
whole place is

579
00:34:00,272 --> 00:34:02,173
their spiderweb. Come
on. Let's go, let's go.

580
00:34:02,340 --> 00:34:04,275
We got to go. Not
everyone wants your help,

581
00:34:04,409 --> 00:34:05,502
Jim Gordon.

582
00:34:06,244 --> 00:34:07,764
Detective Gordon,
your hand's bleeding.

583
00:34:09,347 --> 00:34:10,474
We need to leave.

584
00:34:11,116 --> 00:34:12,116
Come on.

585
00:34:12,784 --> 00:34:14,150
(dog barking in distance)

586
00:34:14,319 --> 00:34:15,548
How many bullets you got left?

587
00:34:16,021 --> 00:34:17,021
Two.

588
00:34:26,798 --> 00:34:28,061
(ignition sputtering)

589
00:34:28,199 --> 00:34:30,225
(engine revving)

590
00:34:40,245 --> 00:34:41,679
SYKES: Looky here, boys!

591
00:34:43,715 --> 00:34:44,715
I'll tell you what,

592
00:34:46,284 --> 00:34:48,185
you give me my workers back,

593
00:34:48,753 --> 00:34:50,722
and I'll let you and
your partner go.

594
00:34:56,661 --> 00:34:57,822
I'm just kidding.

595
00:34:58,229 --> 00:34:59,527
Of course I'm not gonna do that.

596
00:35:00,065 --> 00:35:01,363
I'm gonna kill you all!

597
00:35:03,702 --> 00:35:05,136
WOMAN: Wait just a minute,

598
00:35:05,604 --> 00:35:06,765
please.

599
00:35:10,375 --> 00:35:12,207
The prize for this man's head

600
00:35:12,477 --> 00:35:13,477
is mine.

601
00:35:25,523 --> 00:35:26,547
How is she?

602
00:35:27,726 --> 00:35:28,726
Not great.

603
00:35:29,594 --> 00:35:30,391
I mean, she hasn't said a peep

604
00:35:30,528 --> 00:35:31,552
since you've been gone.

605
00:35:34,232 --> 00:35:35,359
You all right?

606
00:35:35,634 --> 00:35:36,761
Did you find the witch?

607
00:35:38,136 --> 00:35:39,502
It was Ivy.

608
00:35:45,310 --> 00:35:45,834
What's that?

609
00:35:46,311 --> 00:35:48,143
Ivy said it could help Selina.

610
00:35:49,447 --> 00:35:50,210
What, and you trust her?

611
00:35:50,348 --> 00:35:51,611
What choice do I have?

612
00:35:52,183 --> 00:35:54,414
Listen, I want to help
Selina as much as you,

613
00:35:54,552 --> 00:35:56,817
but Ivy is a maniacal,
cold-hearted killer.

614
00:35:57,155 --> 00:35:59,351
- You know that,
don't you?
- Give it to me.

615
00:36:05,497 --> 00:36:07,125
Selina, I have doubts.

616
00:36:08,600 --> 00:36:10,865
Bruce, I was willing
to kill myself yesterday.

617
00:36:11,369 --> 00:36:12,701
Nothing's changed since then.

618
00:36:12,837 --> 00:36:15,830
So if Ivy wants to kill me,

619
00:36:17,208 --> 00:36:18,471
she can have at it.

620
00:36:26,484 --> 00:36:28,180
What do I do, just swallow it?

621
00:36:28,720 --> 00:36:29,720
Yeah.

622
00:36:43,334 --> 00:36:44,495
(sighs)

623
00:36:46,404 --> 00:36:47,565
Still here.

624
00:36:47,772 --> 00:36:48,772
(chuckles)

625
00:36:53,344 --> 00:36:56,246
I know Ivy's lost her mind.

626
00:36:56,481 --> 00:36:57,481
But...

627
00:36:58,183 --> 00:36:59,583
after her mom and dad died,

628
00:36:59,818 --> 00:37:01,309
she was just...

629
00:37:01,820 --> 00:37:03,220
sleeping on the streets.

630
00:37:04,522 --> 00:37:06,548
And it was a cold winter, and...

631
00:37:07,258 --> 00:37:09,352
she started to get really sick.

632
00:37:10,328 --> 00:37:11,853
So I...

633
00:37:14,632 --> 00:37:17,295
took her under my wing, I guess,

634
00:37:19,404 --> 00:37:20,404
and...

635
00:37:20,638 --> 00:37:22,504
showed her where to get food,

636
00:37:23,742 --> 00:37:25,836
where to get a
roof over her head.

637
00:37:27,912 --> 00:37:28,675
And after some time,

638
00:37:28,813 --> 00:37:30,543
she started to get
color in her face.

639
00:37:32,417 --> 00:37:33,441
(chuckles)

640
00:37:35,386 --> 00:37:36,786
And I just...

641
00:37:37,622 --> 00:37:39,523
kept checking in on her.

642
00:37:41,626 --> 00:37:43,390
Almost every day.

643
00:37:47,699 --> 00:37:49,429
She may look old now, but...

644
00:37:50,401 --> 00:37:52,734
she'll always be
that little girl to me.

645
00:37:58,977 --> 00:38:00,605
(shuddering)

646
00:38:00,745 --> 00:38:02,270
- No, no, no, Selina.
- ALFRED: Doctor!

647
00:38:02,447 --> 00:38:03,745
- Selina.
- Doctor!

648
00:38:03,882 --> 00:38:04,882
Selina, stay with me.

649
00:38:04,983 --> 00:38:07,248
- (whimpering)
- Stay back. Give us room.

650
00:38:07,452 --> 00:38:08,452
No, Selina.

651
00:38:08,987 --> 00:38:10,546
DOCTOR: She's burning up.

652
00:38:11,556 --> 00:38:13,252
Pulse is low. What happened?

653
00:38:13,491 --> 00:38:14,982
Oh, God, what have I done?

654
00:38:19,297 --> 00:38:20,663
Put it down, Knucklehead!

655
00:38:20,932 --> 00:38:23,697
You two clowns ain't got a
single bullet between you.

656
00:38:24,302 --> 00:38:25,302
Wrong.

657
00:38:25,370 --> 00:38:26,394
I got two.

658
00:38:27,605 --> 00:38:28,605
Prove it.

659
00:38:28,807 --> 00:38:30,605
I won't say it again, freak.

660
00:38:30,775 --> 00:38:33,301
Gordon comes with me.

661
00:38:33,645 --> 00:38:34,772
I'll tell you what!

662
00:38:35,513 --> 00:38:36,981
I'll take his head,
and you can have

663
00:38:37,315 --> 00:38:38,476
the rest of him!

664
00:38:43,988 --> 00:38:46,457
♪♪

665
00:38:50,929 --> 00:38:52,056
(vehicle approaching)

666
00:39:14,452 --> 00:39:15,452
Hi, Jim.

667
00:39:16,054 --> 00:39:17,647
About our last chat...

668
00:39:19,524 --> 00:39:21,459
I may have been a little rash.

669
00:39:22,427 --> 00:39:23,947
This what got you
all hot and bothered?

670
00:39:23,995 --> 00:39:25,987
- They need a bath.
- Crazy bi...

671
00:39:34,005 --> 00:39:35,064
Wow.

672
00:39:35,707 --> 00:39:37,676
Your last bullet,
just for me, huh?

673
00:39:39,110 --> 00:39:40,442
Must be love.

674
00:39:41,012 --> 00:39:42,503
Not all square yet though.

675
00:39:43,348 --> 00:39:45,817
You're gonna help me do
what we all know needs doing.

676
00:39:45,984 --> 00:39:47,043
Oh, yeah? What's that?

677
00:39:48,019 --> 00:39:49,612
Kill Penguin.

678
00:39:52,690 --> 00:39:54,690
How 'bout we table this
until I can get them safely

679
00:39:54,826 --> 00:39:56,658
into the Green
Zone, huh? Come on.

680
00:40:07,071 --> 00:40:08,071
Wow.

681
00:40:09,440 --> 00:40:10,840
You're safe now. Go on.

682
00:40:11,743 --> 00:40:12,904
LUCIUS: You made it.

683
00:40:13,645 --> 00:40:14,806
You had me worried.

684
00:40:15,580 --> 00:40:17,580
All sorts of chatter out
there about people hunting

685
00:40:17,649 --> 00:40:19,140
you down for Penguin's
reward money.

686
00:40:19,784 --> 00:40:21,377
Well, they'll just
have to try harder.

687
00:40:21,819 --> 00:40:24,618
He did have help from
the unlikeliest of places.

688
00:40:25,390 --> 00:40:26,619
You're welcome.

689
00:40:27,792 --> 00:40:29,420
Show me what you got.

690
00:40:30,628 --> 00:40:31,628
Nice place.

691
00:40:31,696 --> 00:40:34,757
250 apartments. Running
water, hot and cold.

692
00:40:34,966 --> 00:40:36,696
Gas. No electricity yet.

693
00:40:36,901 --> 00:40:37,925
Is there a bar?

694
00:40:41,172 --> 00:40:43,004
LUCIUS: Once the kids
we liberated moved in,

695
00:40:43,141 --> 00:40:44,666
word got out pretty
fast that there was

696
00:40:44,809 --> 00:40:46,175
a safe place to
live in the city.

697
00:40:46,844 --> 00:40:48,836
Citizens are heading
here in droves.

698
00:40:50,815 --> 00:40:53,182
This place will be
full by sundown.

699
00:40:55,119 --> 00:40:56,485
Then we'll find another.

700
00:40:56,955 --> 00:40:59,015
I just want to thank
you, Captain Gordon.

701
00:40:59,457 --> 00:41:01,926
My family, we've been drifting
from one place to the next

702
00:41:02,060 --> 00:41:03,494
ever since the blackout.

703
00:41:04,095 --> 00:41:05,461
You've delivered us.

704
00:41:09,834 --> 00:41:11,097
Seriously?

705
00:41:11,803 --> 00:41:13,465
I'll see you around, killer.

706
00:41:14,505 --> 00:41:16,838
We have some unfinished
business, you and I.

707
00:41:19,110 --> 00:41:21,875
DOCTOR: Whatever she
took put her body into shock.

708
00:41:22,013 --> 00:41:23,208
Her temperature skyrocketed.

709
00:41:23,548 --> 00:41:25,676
Her WBC count
was off the charts.

710
00:41:25,783 --> 00:41:30,016
Then, two hours ago,
everything stabilized.

711
00:41:30,555 --> 00:41:32,080
I have no idea why.

712
00:41:32,190 --> 00:41:35,922
She was still in a lot of
pain, so we sedated her.

713
00:41:36,661 --> 00:41:38,005
She's been sleeping
for a while now.

714
00:41:38,029 --> 00:41:40,589
I think it'd be best to
come back in the morning.

715
00:41:41,766 --> 00:41:43,462
Thank you, Doctor.

716
00:41:46,871 --> 00:41:48,391
Right. Master Bruce,
I think we should,

717
00:41:48,539 --> 00:41:49,539
uh...

718
00:41:50,708 --> 00:41:51,828
we should get some shut-eye.

719
00:41:52,944 --> 00:41:53,944
Come on.

720
00:42:04,155 --> 00:42:07,148
♪♪

721
00:42:18,870 --> 00:42:20,031
Bruce.

722
00:42:27,512 --> 00:42:28,844
It's a miracle.

723
00:42:32,050 --> 00:42:33,050
How do you feel?

724
00:42:33,084 --> 00:42:35,280
(wind blowing)

725
00:42:37,822 --> 00:42:39,051
Different.

726
00:42:41,159 --> 00:42:42,159
Any pain?

727
00:42:42,994 --> 00:42:43,994
No.

728
00:42:47,265 --> 00:42:49,291
Selina, I thought
I'd killed you.

729
00:42:51,069 --> 00:42:52,537
I'm better.

730
00:42:55,106 --> 00:42:57,598
Even better than
before, in fact.
